  "id": "COMPOUND:31978 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but coherent pathway linking the compound (1R,2R,4S,7Z,11R)-4,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-3,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.02,4]tetradec-7-en-13-one to M-phase phosphoprotein 8. The compound is identified as a target of carboxylesterase 2, which is itself targeted by cimetidine. Cimetidine is known to modulate the activity of carboxylesterase 2, and this enzyme is also a target of another compound, [(1R,2R,4S,5S,9R,10S,12S,13R,16R)-2,12-dihydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)-5,9-dimethyl-14-methylidene-15-oxo-16-tetracyclo[11.2.1.01,10.04,9]hexadecanyl] acetate, which in turn targets M-phase phosphoprotein 8. Additionally, the compound is linked to VMRC-LCP, which is targeted by 7-Angeloylechinatine, which also targets M-phase phosphoprotein 8. These findings suggest that the compound may act through a series of enzymatic interactions, potentially modulating the activity of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through the regulation of carboxylesterase 2 and other enzymes. The evidence supports a mechanism involving enzyme targeting and downstream effects on the M-phase phosphoprotein, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
